            "title": "Wall Street vs. Toyota: Elliott's $30 Billion Showdown Sends Shockwaves Through Japan Inc.",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "Elliott Investment Management has been stepping up engagement with asset managers and institutional investors in Japan as it builds momentum around its challenge to the 4.7 trillion proposal to take Toyota Industries (TYIDY) private, according to people familiar with the discussions.  After accumulating a roughly 5% stake, the activist fund led by Paul Singer (Trades, Portfolio) has been meeting with domestic shareholders to convey concerns that the offer may not fully capture the company's underlying value.  Since late August, however, Toyota Industries' shares have traded above the offer price and have recently stood more than 1,500 higher, a dynamic that could be interpreted as investors positioning for a possible increase while reducing the incentive to tender into the current terms.",
